	(footprint "multi_fpga:Adafruit_FT232H"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "245d8bf4-6cee-411e-9314-afb60730d6cc")
		(at 156.6 143.6 180)
		(descr "Adafruit FT232H USB-C breakout (PID 2264), mounted via 2x11 0.1in header strips -- pad grid/board outline adapted from the community footprint at github.com/jgait/adafruit-ft232h-kicad-footprint (cross-checked against Adafruit's own pin descriptions at learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-ft232h-breakout/pinouts and the user-supplied schematic docs/components_FT232H_sch.png), renumbered 1-22 to match this project's existing FT232H_BRK schematic symbol pin numbering exactly: pin1=3V, pin2=5V, pin3=GND, pins4-11=D0-D7, pin12=GND, pins13-22=C9,C8,C7,C6,C5,C4,C3,C2,C1,C0. Only D0-D7 and C0-C3 (as RXF#/TXE#/RD#/WR# in FT245 sync FIFO mode) are wired in this design; the rest (3V, 5V, 2nd GND, C4-C9) are real pad positions intentionally left unconnected, matching Adafruit's own guidance that the 3V/GND pins can be left disconnected. 3D model is the user-supplied lib/Adafruit_FT232H/Adafruit_FT232H_Original_1.STEP -- the raw STEP has the board modeled lying on its long-edge side with a slight (~7deg) in-plane skew, not flat/right-side-up; the (rotate -90deg Z) and (offset 33.32 -48.82 0) were both reverse-engineered empirically (measuring rendered pin-hole pitch/position and mounting-hole alignment against the pad grid above) since no CAD alignment reference was provided with the model; an earlier calibration attempt (-97.055deg) left an uncorrected ~7deg residual skew visible on close inspection, fixed by re-measuring against the two mounting-hole centers directly. Re-verify visually if the STEP file is ever replaced or the footprint rotation changes.")
		(tags "FT232H breakout USB-C Adafruit 2264")
		(property "Reference" "A6"
			(at 0 -22 180)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(uuid "398a586c-bcc7-4ff6-8295-1e72ef270a6e")
