	(footprint "multi_fpga:ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "79582753-07dc-43a3-9558-11bfd4b617fd")
		(at 148.5 66.225)
		(descr "ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR, 12.288 MHz HCMOS TCXO, 3.3V, 5.0x3.2mm 4-pad SMD -- real vendor footprint/pinout, converted from lib/ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR/OSC_ECS-TXO-5032-122.8-TR.kicad_mod (SnapEDA, sourced from ECS's own mechanical drawing). Pin 1 = N/C (VCONT on the VC-TCXO variant only -- this part is the plain TXO, so pin 1 is genuinely unused), pin 2 = GND, pin 3 = Output, pin 4 = VDD, per ecsxtal.com/store/pdf/ECS-TXO-5032.pdf p.2. 3D model Y offset (-0.85mm) was reverse-engineered empirically by rendering and visually centering the body over all 4 pads -- the vendor STEP's own origin isn't at its geometric center/pad-plane, and no alignment dimension was given in the datasheet; re-check visually if the STEP file is ever replaced.")
